<newsitem itemid="163279" id="root" date="1996-11-04" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Lion Match raises interim shr, div.</title>
<headline>Lion Match raises interim shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     41.4	  vs  36.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 12.5	  vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   18.82	 vs  16.65</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   25.81	 vs  23.41</p>
<p>    Tax			  6.99	 vs   6.76</p>
<p>    Turnover		  88.05	 vs  84.53</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 31</p>
<p>on register Nov 29</p>
<p>Full name: The Lion Match Company Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that despite recent inflationary pressure, further modest growth in private consumption expenditure should continue to support consumer demand for Lion's products. Together with actions taken to normalise production at the Durban match factory, this should enable a satisfactory increase in earnings for the full year to be achieved.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
